WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.697
Mike Duffy.

00:00:01.647 --> 00:00:03.329
Pamela Wallin.

00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:05.079
Patrick Brazeau.

00:00:05.079 --> 00:00:06.818
Three senators.

00:00:06.818 --> 00:00:11.477
Ninety thousand dollars in inappropriate housing expense claims from Duffy alone.

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:18.170
The Prime Minister's Chief of Staff — Nigel Wright — wrote a personal cheque for over ninety thousand dollars to cover it up.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.636
Deloitte conducted the audit in 2013.

00:00:21.636 --> 00:00:23.761
Four senators implicated.

00:00:23.761 --> 00:00:28.818
Multiple acquittals despite audit findings — jurisdictional and procedural loopholes.

00:00:28.818 --> 00:00:31.977
Zero criminal convictions for expense abuse.

00:00:31.977 --> 00:00:35.511
The Senate investigated itself... and found nothing wrong.

00:00:35.511 --> 00:00:37.045
Unelected.

00:00:37.045 --> 00:00:38.670
Unaccountable.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.431
Unapologetic.

00:00:40.431 --> 00:00:49.238
The expense scandal revealed a chamber where public money flows without public consent — and where the mechanisms of accountability are controlled by those being held accountable.
